A||||6||MooCow||Help EGR Tube??||||4
Z||000000||MooCow||10-27-1999||09:50 AM||||Could someone please show me a picture of the EGR Tube in a Fiero. I have no idea what it looks like and I plan on buying a Fiero and want to know if it is cracked. Show me one a V6 Fiero.  Are all years the same?? If not show me it on an 86.  <BR>  All info would help.<P>[This message has been edited by MooCow (edited 10-27-1999).]<p>[This message has been edited by MooCow (edited 10-27-1999).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Linx||10-27-1999||11:47 AM||||which fiero? what engine?||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||10-27-1999||11:55 AM||||There is no EGR tube on the 4 cylinder, only on the V6, because of the way it mounts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||10-27-1999||03:06 PM||||No picture, but it's next to the distributor coming off the egr valve, hidden in a tube of silver insulation material.  I found a crack in mine near the end closest to the valve.  The other end worms down to bolt to the underside of the intake manifold towards the back left side(you know, looking at the engine from behind the car left side) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  If you have small hands it will definately help pipe replacement.  I used the assistance of probes to get mine in.  I lost count how many times I dropped nut trying to get it started.||||reg||6
Z||000004||mshill||10-27-1999||04:05 PM||||Even if you know where it is, the only real way to know if it is cracked or not is to remove it.  The heat blanket that covers it may be hiding a crack.  I thought I had a good one off an 87 GT in the bone yard, but after I got it off, I put my hand over one end and blew into the other only to find a crack about three inches up under the wrap.<P>I have gotten really fast at removing/installing the EGR tube.  Remove the  dist cap and rotor.  I use a 10mm ratcheting boxend wrench (8 bucks at ACE hardware) and it is off in about 5 minutes.  About the same to put it back on.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Thomas||10-29-1999||05:56 AM||||The best Way to control the tube for cracking is:<BR>Start the Engine.<BR>Use a starter pilot and spray it on the tube.<BR>If the Engine begin to run faster -&gt; the tube is cracked.<BR>There is no way to repair the tube. Its made with a special Material from Space Technology.<BR>If you must change the tube, then look for oil mud at the conection from Intake Air manifold and tube.||||reg||10
Z||000006||dogtired||10-29-1999||07:49 AM||||Sorry no photo  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  and hard to describe? If you look at any stock V6 fiero, find the distributor basically the coil is on one side and the EGR tube on the other wrapped in silver colored insulation. It actually runs from the bottom of the red plenum, over past the distributor to the crossover exhaust pipe. I don't remember seeing any clear shots of it on anyones WEB site, probably someone will lead you to one?<BR>BUT I have 2 V6's one of the tubes were cracked (kind of like the driver) and the other is good. The cracked one I removed from the car, removed the insulation wrap and brazed it. I am not a pro as far as welding goes but I would think if you took it to a pro, probably for a lot cheeper than buying a replacement it can be repaired. Just something I did.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
